2026-10-09 18:10:47.627 DEBUG icod.agent.runtime.loop: STEP 1: model responded ->\n  - text: This is a great research topic. Let me lay out how the major platforms architect formulas and what options exist for a system like yours.\n\n## How Excel/Smartsheet/Google Sheets Handle Formulas\n\n### 1. Dependency Graph (DAG) Architecture\nThis is the core pattern used by **all** major spreadsheet engines.\n\n- Each cell with a formula is a **node** in a directed acyclic graph\n- Edges represent dependencies (`=A1+B1` → this node depends on A1 and B1)\n- When a cell changes, only its **downstream dependents** are recalculated (not the entire sheet)\n- Excel pioneered this with its **recalculation engine** — it tracks a dirty flag per cell and walks the DAG topologically\n\n### 2. Formula Pipeline (Parsing → AST → Evaluation)\nEvery formula goes through these stages:\n\n| Stage | What Happens | Example |\n|-------|-------------|---------|\n| **Lexer/Tokenizer** | Breaks formula string into tokens | `=SUM(A1:A3)` → `SUM`, `(`, `A1:A3`, `)` |\n| **Parser** | Builds an Abstract Syntax Tree (AST) | `FunctionCall("SUM", [Range("A1","A3")])` |\n| **Resolver** | Resolves cell/range references to actual values | `A1:A3` → `[10, 20, 30]` |\n| **Evaluator** | Walks the AST, computes results | `SUM([10,20,30])` → `60` |\n| **Formatter** | Formats output based on column type | `60` → `"60"` or `"$60.00"` |\n\n### 3. Where Evaluation Happens — Three Models\n\n**A. Client-Side Only (Excel, Google Sheets)**\n- Formulas parsed and evaluated entirely in the browser/desktop\n- Server stores formula strings, not computed values\n- Pros: Instant feedback, no server load\n- Cons: Can't use server-side data, complex sync for collaboration\n\n**B. Server-Side Only (Airtable, some BI tools)**\n- Client sends formula, server evaluates and returns result\n- Pros: Single source of truth, can access cross-table data, security\n- Cons: Latency on every keystroke, server compute cost\n\n**C. Hybrid (Smartsheet, modern approach)**\n- Client evaluates for instant preview while editing\n- Server re-evaluates on save for canonical results and cross-sheet references\n- Server stores both the formula string and the last computed value\n- Pros: Fast UX + authoritative server results\n- Cons: Must keep two engines in sync (same function set, same semantics)\n\n## Options for Your App\n\n### Option 1: Embed a JS Formula Engine (Fastest to ship)\nUse an existing library that handles parsing + evaluation:\n\n| Library | Approach | Pros | Cons |\n|---------|----------|------|------|\n| **[Hot-formulajs](https://github.com/handsontable/hyperformula)** | Full engine, 400+ Excel-compatible functions, dependency graph | Battle-tested, open source (GPL), full DAG recalc | GPL license, large bundle (~500KB), opinionated API |\n| **[Formula.js](https://github.com/silentmatt/expr-eval)** / **expr-eval** | Simple math expression evaluator | Tiny, easy to extend | No cell references, no ranges, no built-in functions |\n| **[Jison / PEG.js / Nearley](https://github.com/zaach/jison)** | Parser generator — build your own grammar | Full control, learn a lot | Significant effort, must build everything yourself |\n| **Custom recursive-descent parser** | Hand-write lexer + parser + evaluator | Full control, no deps, exact fit for your data model | Weeks of work, must handle edge cases yourself |\n\n### Option 2: Custom Engine (Most control, best fit)\nBuild a lightweight formula engine tailored to your architecture:\n\n```\nFormula string: "=SUM({col_id_1}) + {col_id_2}"\n        ↓\n    Lexer → tokens\n        ↓\n    Parser → AST nodes\n        ↓\n    Evaluator → walks AST using row values from DB\n        ↓\n    Result stored on row (or computed on-the-fly)\n```\n\nKey design decisions:\n- **Reference model**: Column-based (`{Column Name}`) vs cell-based (`A1`) — Smartsheet uses column references since rows are records, not a grid\n- **Function set**: Start small (SUM, AVG, COUNT, MIN, MAX, IF, CONCAT) and expand\n- **Evaluation trigger**: On row save (server-side) vs on every cell change (client-side)\n- **Storage**: Store formula in one row, computed va... (+1601 chars)
